HZK12, HZK14, and HZK16 are copied byte-for-byte from the upstream font/
directory. Inkwire uses its own Go loader and does not include the upstream C++
decoder. Other HZK styles and sizes are intentionally excluded so the UI keeps
one consistent glyph style.

The MONACO files are 1-bit ASCII strikes generated from macOS
/System/Library/Fonts/Monaco.ttf with Pillow 12.3.0, integer coordinates, and
no antialiasing. MONACO10 keeps the exact 8x12, baseline 10, advance 6 setup
that was verified on the physical tag. The retained sizes are 10, 12, 14, and
16px; Monaco 10/12/14 are paired with HZK 12/14/16 respectively.

